<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: Czech real Nov farm revenues down 2.6 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Czech real Nov farm revenues down 2.6 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Total revenues from Czech farming enterprises fell 2.6 percent year-on-year in November in inflation-adjusted terms, putting revenues for January-November down 0.5 percent, the Czech Statistical Office said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The figures refer to the sale of own goods and services in total.  </p>
<p>Revenues from agricultural production alone were down 3.6 percent year-on-year in November and down 1.3 percent in the January-November period.</p>
<p>The Statistical Office added that the number of workers employed in the farm sector fell in absolute terms to 142,309 from 146,550 in October and was 4.8 percent lower than in November 1995.</p>
<p>The average monthly farm wage was 8,835 crowns, down from 8,956 in October.</p>
<p>-- Robin Shepherd, Prague Newsroom, 42-2-2423-0003</p>
